        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/332036?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Please remember to create inline comments for discussions to keep this RFC manageable and discussion trees resolveable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/oli-obk/rfcs/blob/const-trait-impl/text/0000-const-trait-impls.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tracking:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"544416304\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/67792\">rust-lang/rust#67792</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3762",
            "title": "Make trait methods callable in const contexts",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-21T10:11:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-13T16:44:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "oli-obk",
                "url": "https://github.com/oli-obk"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76854355?u=c8a002ee3c70f41a556c7dff250e0abf1244ec76&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h1 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h1>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The addition of <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">Cargo.toml</code>. This field is an array of <code class=\"notranslate\">target-triple</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">cfg</code> specifications that restricts the set of targets which a package supports. Packages must meet the <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code> of their dependencies, and they can only be built for targets that satisfy their <code class=\"notranslate\">supported-targets</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/carloskiki/rfcs/blob/master/text/3759-cargo-supported-targets.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3759",
            "title": "RFC: Allow packages to specify a set of supported targets",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-15T02:30:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-01-08T19:43:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "carloskiki",
                "url": "https://github.com/carloskiki"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6120103?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Special case struct patterns containing only a rest pattern (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">Foo { .. }</code>) so that they can match values of any type with the appropriate name, not just structs (e.g., it could match an <code class=\"notranslate\">enum Foo</code> value). This is done so that structs containing only private fields can be changed to other types without breaking backwards compatibility.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/rest-patterns-foo-should-match-non-struct-types/21607\" rel=\"nofollow\">Prior discussion on IRLO</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/theemathas/rfcs/blob/rest_pattern_matches_non_struct/text/3753-rest-pattern-matches-non-struct.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3753",
            "title": "RFC: `Foo { .. }` pattern matches non-struct types",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-10T15:09:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-31T10:47:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "theemathas",
                "url": "https://github.com/theemathas"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4459874?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC is largely the work of <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/rylev/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/rylev\">@rylev</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/chriswailes/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/chriswailes\">@chriswailes</a>. As <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3379#issuecomment-1876158423\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3379/hovercard\">suggested by @tmandry</a> I have stripped it down to an MVP that just adds <code class=\"notranslate\">os_version_min</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisDenton/rfcs/blob/os-min-version/text/3750-cfg-os-version-min.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3750",
            "title": "RFC: cfg_os_version_min",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-11T13:59:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-27T11:09:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ChrisDenton",
                "url": "https://github.com/ChrisDenton"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/653604?u=bcaaafaa0439ac0006d5e4aff450ab0b826bc5ec&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add a new environment variable <code class=\"notranslate\">CARGO_CHECK</code> that is set to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> when running <code class=\"notranslate\">cargo check</code> so build scripts can skip expensive compilation steps that are unnecessary for Rust type checking, such as compiling external C++ code in cxx based projects.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/akiselev/rfcs/blob/cargo-check-env/text/3748-cargo_check_environment_variable.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3748",
            "title": "RFC: Set CARGO_CHECK environment variable when type checking",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-04T11:41:09.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-21T04:51:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "akiselev",
                "url": "https://github.com/akiselev"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185516564?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">issue for this RFC <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/134475\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/134475/hovercard\">rust-lang/rust#134475</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes checking for <code class=\"notranslate\">T: Sized</code> in required trait methods (which do not check for some reason) which will be a future compatibility lint</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/ionicmc-rs/rfcs/blob/master/text/3696-unsized-params-in-traits.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3745",
            "title": "unsized params in traits",
            "date_modified": "2024-12-22T13:39:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-18T21:11:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ionicmc-rs",
                "url": "https://github.com/ionicmc-rs"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128307220?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">As discussed previously:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://smallcultfollowing.com/babysteps/blog/2014/05/13/focusing-on-ownership/\" rel=\"nofollow\">2014 Blog post</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/lack-of-mut-in-bindings-as-a-deny-by-default-lint/15818\" rel=\"nofollow\">2021 IRLO thread</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/stream/213817-t-lang/topic/Idea.3A.20Downgrade.20.22immutable.20variable.E2.80.9C.20errors.20to.20lints\" rel=\"nofollow\">Zulip thread</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mutation of non-mutable locals arguably resembles a lint more than a hard error.  Converting it to a configurable lint has the potential to reduce friction and more clearly distinguish it from Rust's more fundamental type system restrictions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Implementing this is less effort than you might expect: the borrow checker already has separate code paths for handling local variables.  I've written a proof-of-concept for the change as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/134233\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/pull/134233/hovercard\">this pull request</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/em-tg/rfcs/blob/emy/text/3742-mutate-non-mutable-locals.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3742",
            "title": "Convert \"reassignment of immutable local\" and \"mutable borrow of immutable local\" from a hard error to a deny-by-default lint",
            "date_modified": "2024-12-20T15:36:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-15T19:26:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "em-tg",
                "url": "https://github.com/em-tg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22172241?u=aaead0ae99d8d3dfba8f4b2dcda9f176228c8d97&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Rust does not allow destructuring types which implement the <code class=\"notranslate\">Drop</code> trait. This means that moving data out of such types is hard and error prone. The rationale is that once fields are moved out, the type's <code class=\"notranslate\">Drop</code> implementation cannot run, which can be undesired. This RFC proposes to allow destructuring anyway, in certain situations.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">drop_type_destructuring</code> adds a new built-in macro, <code class=\"notranslate\">destructure</code>. You can use this macro to destructure types that implement <code class=\"notranslate\">Drop</code>. For example, assuming <code class=\"notranslate\">Foo</code> is a type that implements <code class=\"notranslate\">Drop</code> and has fields <code class=\"notranslate\">a</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">b</code>, you could write the following:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"fn example(x: Foo) {\n    destructure!(let Foo { a, b: _ } = x);\n    // yay we own `a` now, we can even drop it!\n    drop(a);\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">example</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">x</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">Foo</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">destructure</span><span class=\"pl-en\">!</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Foo</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> a<span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> b<span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> _ <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span> = x<span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c\">// yay we own `a` now, we can even drop it!</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">drop</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span>a<span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Written together with <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/WaffleLapkin/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/WaffleLapkin\">@WaffleLapkin</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/jdonszelmann/rfcs/blob/drop-type-destructuring/text/3738-drop-type-destructuring.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3738",
            "title": "Drop type destructuring",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-08T01:32:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-08T00:34:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jdonszelmann",
                "url": "https://github.com/jdonszelmann"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19915050?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Allow annotating functions with <code class=\"notranslate\">#[must_use = false]</code> to suppress any warning generated due to its return type being marked as <code class=\"notranslate\">#[must_use]</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-must-use-false/21861\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC on IRLO</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/lolbinarycat/rust-rfcs/blob/must_use-false/text/3737-must_use-false.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3737",
            "title": "#[must_use = false]",
            "date_modified": "2025-02-16T00:18:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-07T18:23:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "lolbinarycat",
                "url": "https://github.com/lolbinarycat"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130038091?u=ee14d5421ebc534c38bc2826c1a38a3d07878657&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes Partial Types as universal and type safe solution to \"partial borrowing\" like problems.<br>\nThis RFC is a third try and it is based on <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3426\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3426/hovercard\">Partial Types (v2) #3426</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\"><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/VitWW/rfcs/blob/partial_types3_mult_min/text/0000-partial_types.md\">Rendered</a></strong></h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Example:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"struct StructABC { a: u32, b: i64, c: f32, }\n\n// function with partial parameter Struct\nfn ref_a (s : &amp; StructABC.{a}) -&gt; &amp;u32 {\n    &amp;s.a\n}\n\nlet s = StructABC {a: 4, b: 7, c: 0.0};\n\n// partial expression, partial reference and partial argument\nlet sa = ref_a(&amp; s.{a});\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">struct</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">StructABC</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">u32</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">b</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">i64</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">c</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">f32</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\">// function with partial parameter Struct</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">ref_a</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">s</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">StructABC</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>a<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> -&gt; <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">u32</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span>s<span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">a</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> s = <span class=\"pl-smi\">StructABC</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">4</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">b</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">7</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">c</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">0.0</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-c\">// partial expression, partial reference and partial argument</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> sa = <span class=\"pl-en\">ref_a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span> s<span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">a</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3736",
            "title": "RFC: Partial Types (v3)",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-21T22:38:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-06T16:58:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "VitWW",
                "url": "https://github.com/VitWW"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/94611769?u=c64b6eb0bd05d503079483eb2aa477cfaf482c16&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/y86-dev/rfcs/blob/field-projection-v2/text/3735-field-projections.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is my second attempt at a field projection RFC, <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3318\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3318/hovercard\">here is the first</a>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add field projections, a very general operation. In simple terms, it is a new operator that turns a generic container type <code class=\"notranslate\">C&lt;T&gt;</code> containing a struct <code class=\"notranslate\">T</code> into a container <code class=\"notranslate\">C&lt;F&gt;</code> where <code class=\"notranslate\">F</code> is a field of the struct <code class=\"notranslate\">T</code>. For example given the struct:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"struct Foo {\n    bar: i32,\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">struct</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">Foo</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">bar</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">i32</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">One can project from <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;mut MaybeUninit&lt;Foo&gt;</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;mut MaybeUninit&lt;i32&gt;</code> by using the new field projection operator:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-rust notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"impl Foo {\n    fn initialize(this: &amp;mut MaybeUninit&lt;Self&gt;) {\n        let bar: &amp;mut MaybeUninit&lt;i32&gt; = this-&gt;bar;\n        bar.write(42);\n    }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">impl</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">Foo</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">fn</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">initialize</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">this</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span><span class=\"pl-k\">mut</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MaybeUninit</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">Self</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">let</span> bar<span class=\"pl-kos\">:</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">&amp;</span><span class=\"pl-k\">mut</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MaybeUninit</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-smi\">i32</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span> = this-&gt;bar<span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n        bar<span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">write</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">42</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Special cases of field projections are pin projections, or projecting raw pointers to fields <code class=\"notranslate\">*mut Foo</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">*mut i32</code> with improved syntax over <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;raw mut (*ptr).bar</code>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3735",
            "title": "[RFC] field projections v2",
            "date_modified": "2025-01-26T13:59:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2024-12-04T10:19:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "y86-dev",
                "url": "https://github.com/y86-dev"
            }
        }
    ]
}